; Ozbound region data: the Yellow Brick Road, eastern stretch.
;
; A region is a level with no [guide]: scenery, resources, signs, houses and exits only (see
; bluebrook.map for the full format). Registered in assets/world/locations.world as
; YELLOW_BRICK_ROAD_EAST. The map is 64 x 64 tiles. The road runs west to east at y = 20, crosses a
; river on a wooden bridge (x = 28-30), and passes a waystation with a roomy house, a garden, and
; two vineyard columns. Its west edge (x = 0, y = 20) is where the path joins Bluebrook's east edge
; in the overworld, so the road is walked straight on from the village; the east end is not open yet. A narrow opening in the northern forest leads to an empty meadow (y = 40-61) kept ready for building out.

[map]
; '.' grass, '=' path, '~' water, 'T' tree, '#' rock, 'F' fence, 'S' signpost,
; 'g' garden bed, 'v' vineyard row (both block movement; walk the grass lanes between).
; Houses are not drawn here: the [houses] section stamps walls, a doorway, and floor.
